Let HarmonyOS report its location permission to Chromium's system layer.

A site granted geolocation while the app itself holds no location permission
gets a prompt it cannot act on: the page is told yes, and the platform then
refuses. Chromium already handles this -- GeolocationPermissionContextSystem
resolves such a request to CONTENT_SETTING_BLOCK before any prompt is shown --
but only where os_level_geolocation_permission_supported is set, which was
ChromeOS, Apple and Windows.

Turning it on for OHOS also brings in GeolocationSystemPermissionManager, whose
constructor and observer are themselves behind the flag; there is no way to
register the manager first and enable the behaviour afterwards. So both land
together, and rolling back means reverting the one GN condition rather than
code. GeolocationProviderImpl reads the manager under the same flag, which is
why the manager is created in NotifyAuraShellBrowserStarted, before anything
can ask for a position.

The source implementation itself is new and lives in the overlay, at
chrome/browser/ui/ohos/system_geolocation_source_ohos.{h,cc}; only its entry in
the sources list needs a patch. That hunk is anchored on the is_ohos block
chromium-154-harmonyos.patch adds, so it applies to the tree as that patch
leaves it, not to a pristine one.

The permission state comes from the shell over the existing command channel.
The NDK can read it, but only through libability_runtime, which
//chrome/browser does not link, while ArkTS already has abilityAccessCtrl.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-system-geolocation-permission.patch

diff --git a/services/device/public/cpp/geolocation/buildflags.gni b/services/device/public/cpp/geolocation/buildflags.gni
--- a/services/device/public/cpp/geolocation/buildflags.gni
+++ b/services/device/public/cpp/geolocation/buildflags.gni
@@ -9,5 +9,6 @@
   # Specifies if we support the OS level global geolocation permission for the
   # current platform. This is exposed with the macro
   # OS_LEVEL_GEOLOCATION_PERMISSION_SUPPORTED.
-  os_level_geolocation_permission_supported = is_chromeos || is_apple || is_win
+  os_level_geolocation_permission_supported =
+      is_chromeos || is_apple || is_win || is_ohos
 }
diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -881,6 +881,8 @@ source_set("core") {
   if (is_ohos) {
     sources += [
       "ui/ohos/aura_shell_runtime_bridge.cc",
       "ui/ohos/aura_shell_runtime_bridge.h",
+      "ui/ohos/system_geolocation_source_ohos.cc",
+      "ui/ohos/system_geolocation_source_ohos.h",
     ]
   }
 
